09. DEMO DATA AND PERSISTENCE
==================================================

Implement one shared typed data layer.

Suggested:
React Context or Zustand.
LocalStorage for demo persistence.

Data structures:
AppointmentRequest
CalendarEvent
FollowUp
ActivityLog
DemoSettings

Use deterministic initial sample records.

Provide a reset function.

All records must be fictional and clearly labeled demo data.

When a new demo appointment request is submitted:
1. Save it to shared demo state.
2. Generate its reference.
3. Make it appear in Requests.
4. Update dashboard counts.
5. Add an activity entry.
6. Keep the state after refresh.

An unconfirmed request should not automatically become a confirmed calendar booking.

After staff confirmation:
- Create/update the calendar event.
- Update status.
- Update metrics.
- Add history entry.

After rescheduling:
- Move the event to the selected date/time.
- Update all views.

After cancellation:
- Remove it from confirmed schedule display or show as cancelled.
- Preserve its history.

No fake API calls.
No hardcoded counters disconnected from sample records.
No button that appears to work but does nothing.

